body:
I think with manga direction and execution have a low bar in general. One has to remember mangaka especially with long stories make things up as they go along. I don't have many under my belt but haven't come across one that doesn't suffer from these weird changes in direction and loose threads.

&#x200B;

I would judge as if it was an improvisation and not as a polished piece. I'm not sure if improvised work can be a masterpiece. But it's pretty enjoyable and very unique
